{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2SA",
  "chapter": 8,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And after this it came to pass, that David smote the Philistines, and subdued them: and David took Metheg-ammah out of the hand of the Philistines.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he smote Moab, and measured them with a line, casting them down to the ground; even with two lines he measured to put to death, and with one full line to keep alive. And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Moabites became David's servants, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brought gifts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "David smote also Hadadezer, the son of Rehob, king of Zobah, as he went to recover his border at the river Euphrates.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David took from him a thousand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "chariots",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and seven hundred horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen: and David houghed all the chariot -",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": " horses",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but reserved of them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a hundred chariots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when the Syrians of Damascus came to succor Hadadezer king of Zobah, David slew of the Syrians two and twenty thousand men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then David put garrisons in Syria of Damascus: and the Syrians became servants to David, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brought gifts. And the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And from Betah, and from Berothai, cities of Hadadezer, king David took very much brass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Toi king of Hamath heard that David had smitten all the host of Hadadezer,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Toi sent Joram his son to king David, to salute him, and to bless him, because he had fought against Hadadezer, and smitten him: (for Hadadezer had wars with Toi) and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Joram",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brought with him vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and vessels of brass:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which also king David dedicated to the LORD, with the silver and gold that he had dedicated of all nations which he subdued;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of Syria, and of Moab, and of the children of Ammon, and of the Philistines, and of Amalek, and of the spoil of Hadadezer son of Rehob, king of Zobah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David made ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a name when he returned from smiting of the Syrians in the valley of Salt, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " eighteen thousand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he put garrisons in Edom; throughout all Edom he put garrisons, and all they of Edom became David's servants. And the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David reigned over all Israel; and David executed judgment and justice to all his people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joab the son of Zeruiah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the host; and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " recorder;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Zadok the son of Ahitub, and Ahimelech the son of Abiathar, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the priests: and Seraiah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the scribe;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2SA.8.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2SA.8.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was over",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " both the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and David's sons were chief rulers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
